            "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0",
            "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fan_Mountains300.jpg",
            "fame": 18,
            "description": {
                "fr": null,
                "en": "The Fann Mountains (Tajik: Кӯҳҳои Фон, romanized: Kúhhoi Fon) are part of the western Pamir-Alay mountain system in Tajikistan's Sughd Province, between the Zarafshan Range to the north and the Gissar Range to the south. In an east-west direction, they extend from the Fan Darya to the Archimaydan River."
            }
